    "clue_custom_text1": "There was exactly one person beside a table.",
    "clue_custom_text2": "There was exactly one person beside a barrel.",
    "clue_custom_text3": "",
    "player_hint_1_en": "(G) is in The Desert since she is in the top row, but cannot be on a path tile per (D)'s clue. This means that (G) is alone with (I) in The Desert. This isolates (E) to the sand tiles in R6. Cross out the rest of R6.",
    "player_hint_2_en": "(B) is in a chair either in R3 or R10. (A) is one row south of someone on a flag, which means he is either in R3 or R10. This means that (A) and (B) will occupy those rows in some configuration. This sets (H) to R5 C3 or R2 C10, block the intersecting squares R5 C10 and R2 C3.",
    "player_hint_3_en": "Amongst C7 - C9, (E) must be there on a sand tile, one person is beside a table, and one person is beside a barrel. This means that no one else can occupy those columns.",
    "player_hint_4_en": "This isolates (B) to R3 C4 since she cannot occupy the chairs in C7 and C9. This means (A) is in R10, which also means someone must occupy the flag in R9 C1. Cross out all squares that intersect with R9 C1.",
    "player_hint_5_en": "This isolates (I) to R2, which isolates (H) to R5 C3. This isolates (G), then isolates (I). This isolates (D) to the last path square. This isolates (A). This isolates the unknown person beside the table to R8 C7, which then isolates (E).",
    "player_hint_6_en": "Because (F) has to be alone, she is in R9 C1. (C) has to be beside the table since he cannot be in a corner. This leaves (V) next to the barrel in the Barrels with (E). Elyana is the murderer!"
  },
